From db9abeeb87bbdbcc9b4a55841f30fb161af95c21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:37:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: move to version 1 of kodi_web_v1

kodi_web_v1 is reset to version 1 before its first release. Kodi now
refuses a web profile identifier the protocol does not allow, stops a
web app whose scripts or content filters the client cannot apply and
says so in a notification, and closes the app when its page asks to
leave. The media state a page reports drives HasVideo(), HasAudio()
and the playback speed, so the screensaver and display power rules
treat a paused or audio-only page as they would a paused video or
music. Content filters in a web profile directory are read in Adblock
Plus syntax, from *.txt, and shared content filter lists are handed to
the client over the manager.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
